---
/**
 * about.astro — About page
 * Follows template in docs/CONTENT_GUIDE.md section 7
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../config';
---

<Base
  metaTitle={`About ${SITE_CONFIG.siteName}`}
  metaDescription={`Learn more about ${SITE_CONFIG.siteName}, our mission to provide accurate, transparent material calculators, and our editorial standards.`}
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>About {SITE_CONFIG.siteName}</h1>

    <p>
      {SITE_CONFIG.siteName} offers free, transparent calculators that help US homeowners
      and DIYers estimate how much material they need for common home and garden projects
      such as mulch, gravel, concrete, paint, and flooring.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we built this site</h2>
    <p>
      Planning a weekend outdoor or home improvement project often begins with a simple question:
      "How many bags do I need?" Too many online calculators hide their math behind lead-generation
      forms or require accounts. We believe you should get a dependable number instantly, with
      complete visibility into how that number was calculated.
    </p>

    <h2>How our calculators work</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculator on this site runs entirely in your web browser. No measurements or numbers
      you enter are sent to a server or saved to a database. Our formulas use standard geometric
      conversions and typical commercial product sizes (such as 2-cubic-foot mulch bags or 80-pound
      concrete bags). We provide editable assumption panels so you can adjust dimensions, bag yields,
      and waste allowances to match your specific supplier's product specifications.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence and accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We are an independent project and are not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by
      any home improvement retailer, building material manufacturer, or landscaping quarry.
      Our priorities are mathematical correctness and clear, original explanations.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions or corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you spot a mathematical discrepancy, an outdated product specification, or have a suggestion
      for a new calculator, please email us directly at
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE_CONFIG.contactEmail}`}>{SITE_CONFIG.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .prose-page h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .prose-page h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .prose-page p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
</style>
